wifi: mt76: mt7925: keep the join ROC until the station is authorized

When a non-MLO station associates, mgd_complete_tx() aborts the join ROC as
soon as the association succeeds, which is right before the supplicant sends
message 2 of the 4-way handshake. With the abort that close to message 2, the
adapter acknowledges nothing the AP sends for the next several ms: the AP
sends message 3 and its seven retries within about 5 ms, none is acknowledged,
and the handshake ends with reason 15 (4WAY_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT).

Keep the ROC after a successful (re)association on a non-MLD station interface
and release it when the station is authorized, on disassociation, or when the
station is removed. The ROC timer still ends it if none of that happens. MLD
interfaces keep the old behaviour.

Upstream tested this on an MT7925U (USB) against a FRITZ!Box 5690 Pro on a
6 GHz-only, non-MLO SSID, kernel 7.2.3: 8 of 84 handshakes completed
unpatched and 30 of 30 patched. Nobody has reported a run on an MT7927.

Fixes: c948b5da6bbe ("wifi: mt76: mt7925: add Mediatek Wi-Fi7 driver for mt7925 chips")

Backported from upstream commit ac22c8c723c62013dd45b74e32249fc877c86fe0.
It first appears in v7.4-rc1 and is not in the 7.3.y stable series, so the
kernel 7.3.5 tarball this package builds from does not have it. It needs the
roc_join_held flag added by the previous patch.

Context regenerated against the 7.3.5 tree with this package's AP-mode
patches and the previous patch already applied.

--- a/mt7925/main.c
+++ b/mt7925/main.c
@@ -1256,6 +1256,13 @@
 {
 	struct mt792x_dev *dev = container_of(mdev, struct mt792x_dev, mt76);
 	struct ieee80211_link_sta *link_sta = &sta->deflink;
+	struct mt792x_vif *mvif = (struct mt792x_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
+
+	if (mvif->roc_join_held && !sta->tdls &&
+	    (ev == MT76_STA_EVENT_AUTHORIZE || ev == MT76_STA_EVENT_DISASSOC)) {
+		mvif->roc_join_held = false;
+		mt7925_abort_roc(mvif->phy, &mvif->bss_conf);
+	}
 
 	switch (ev) {
 	case MT76_STA_EVENT_ASSOC:
@@ -1451,6 +1458,7 @@
 
 	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION) {
 		mvif->wep_sta = NULL;
+		mvif->roc_join_held = false;
 		ewma_rssi_init(&mvif->bss_conf.rssi);
 	}
 
@@ -2103,6 +2111,19 @@
 {
 	struct mt792x_vif *mvif = (struct mt792x_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
 
+	/* Keep the join ROC until the station is authorized, so that it
+	 * covers the 4-way handshake. mt7925_mac_sta_event() releases it.
+	 * On MLD, the active ROC is the MLO ROC, which must be released
+	 * before the link activation work sets its own.
+	 */
+	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION && !ieee80211_vif_is_mld(vif) &&
+	    info->success &&
+	    (info->subtype == IEEE80211_STYPE_ASSOC_REQ ||
+	     info->subtype == IEEE80211_STYPE_REASSOC_REQ)) {
+		mvif->roc_join_held = true;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	mt7925_abort_roc(mvif->phy, &mvif->bss_conf);
 }
 
